    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.21) stands as our clear cornerstone. Even with his lineup spot currently pending, the combination of a favorable matchup against Jacob Lopez (4.67 xERA) and his consistent recency metrics makes him an elite play. **Jackson Merrill** (69.12) also grades out strongly at the #5 spot, benefiting from a soft matchup against Jake Irvin; his ability to contribute across the board\u2014particularly in our scarcity focus, Stolen Bases\u2014makes him an essential high-floor start. While **Gunnar Henderson** (65.79) and **Coby Mayo** (65.57) face a tougher challenge in Joey Cantillo, their park factors and current form provide enough insulation to keep them firmly in the strong start category.\n\nThe decision to keep **Nasim Nunez** (37.54) on the bench was the tightest call of the day. While his sprint speed usually makes him a priority for our Stolen Base targets, the matchup against Nick Pivetta\u2019s 2.85 xERA suppresses his offensive ceiling, and his projected bottom-of-the-order slot creates too much risk for our daily game cap efficiency. Consequently, we are leaning on **Wade Meckler** (51.27) for his superior situational placement at #3 against Brayan Bello. We continue to monitor the status of **Kyle Tucker** (55.52), whose score remains somewhat muted due to the challenge of facing Chase Burns. While the health of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Andy Pages** remains a concern for our long-term depth, the current lineup maximizes our immediate scoring potential against the day's specific pitching rotation.",
